k1q|v|To turn up, or delve in, (earth) with a spade or a hoe; to open, loosen, or break up (the soil) with a spade, or other sharp instrument; to pierce, open, or loosen, as if with a spade. ; To get by digging; as, to dig potatoes, or gold. ; To hollow out, as a well; to form, as a ditch, by removing earth; to excavate; as, to dig a ditch or a well. ; To thrust; to poke. ; To work with a spade or other like implement; to do servile work; to delve. ; To take ore from its bed, in distinction from making excavations in search of ore. ; To work like a digger; to study ploddingly and laboriously. ; A plodding and laborious student.	o:2258,20,1;wrl,16,2~wrl,16,2;2258,20,1	s:1d2v,12,1~1d2v,12,1	d:1kie,6,4~1kie,6,4	D:ibf,47,5;ibb,16,4~ibf,47,5;ibb,16,4
